==Strategy==
This stage combines aggressive pushers with a tanky backliner, and Bakoo makes it difficult to even use meatshields. Fortunately, its greatest defense also happens to be its downfall; Elder Sloth attacks quite infrequently and the Dark enemies have many knockbacks, meaning that he can easily be isolated, [[Freeze|Frozen]] and used as a stepping stone to make quick work of everything here.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]: Bombercat is rather difficult to obtain, but considering [[Bombergirl (Deadly)|Bombergirl]], one of its prerequisite stages, is also locked behind ITF3 completion, all that's needed is some patience to catch [[Bloomin' Brightly (Easy)|the stage]] when given the chance. Able to outrange all Dark enemies here with 100% chance to Freeze them, Bombercat, when backed by meatshields, can shut down their advances and leave them to the mercy of specialist attackers.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: Pizza's Massive Damage ability to Darks allows it to delete them in a few hits, and is crucial in securing victory, as it also outranges all Dark enemies in this stage. With its Wave Attack Talent, Pizza only gets better, and can even hit threats that aren't within range of its initial attack, which can knockback Bakoo, even if she's behind an Elder Sloth.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: With the Extra Money and Move Speed Up Talents, Can Can serves as a cheap, disposable yet powerful attacker that can snipe Doge Darks to provide a surge of income. As Elder Sloth has a long delay between his attacks, Can Can is able to get a few hits in and inflict fairly significant damage.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: Seafarer has fair stats, a long cooldown, 100% chance to Survive a Lethal Strike and has 40% chance to Freeze Aliens. This might not sound like much, but when several are present (and with Talents improving Freeze Chance to 60%) they can easily stunlock Elder Sloth to expose all Dark threats.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]/[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: These disposable LD attackers are always good for accumulating DPS, being useful for the same reason as they are on [[Bombergirl (Deadly)|Bombergirl]] and potentially [[Wrath of the Dreamer (Deadly)|Wrath of the Dreamer]]. They need to be backed by other frontline units while exploiting their LD to snipe Bakoo.
*[[Ancient Egg: N103 (Rare Cat)|Gas Mask Cat]]: While bringing a meatshield is counterintuitive to the stage's main strat, when supported by Long Distance attackers to knock back Bakoo, it can prevent the other Dark peons from pushing towards your other units. Gas Mask Cat is also a ranged meatshield, requiring Bakoo to walk close to it in order to start attacking.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: Jizo's first form is incredibly effective. As a spammable attacker with Massive Damage to Darks, a few of them can quickly whittle down the Dark threats, and can be easily replaced when lost. Jizo certainly needs a fair bit of support to stop Darks from getting to it, but when they are kept at bay, Jizo works wonders.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: With high piercing range and immunity to freeze, you won't have to worry if Bakoo actually gets a hit out. Bakoo does little damage and won't phase Izanagi at all. The high dps also makes it likely that Bakoo will be knocked back before getting a hit out, not that it'll matter for Izanagi anyway.
*[[Akechi Mitsuhide (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Mitsuhide]]: Mitsuhide is good for this stage, given that he has guaranteed Knockback with Long Distance. Make sure none of the Bakoos ever attack, as this guy has no Freeze Immunity.

